WEBVTT

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:30.030
I wish to congratulate the chosen
Phi-Brain children on their victory.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.010
As I suspected, it has come down to you two.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.260
Friendship and love...

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:41.270
I see you have transcended beyond
such ludicrous human emotions.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.700
Damn you, Orpheus!

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:44.770
What are you talking about?

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.770
Kaito Daimon abandoned Gammon
and Freecell to their fates.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.530
With this, you have earned the right...

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.120
The right to challenge the Puzzle of God!

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:04.250
One of you shall become a Phi-Brain
and serve as my new vessel.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.260
Tomorrow you will begin the Puzzle of God.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:11.850
I shall see you then, Phi-Brain children!

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.110
I’ll solve the Puzzle of God by myself.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.640
Raetsel, don’t show up!

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.620
I swear that I’ll seal Orpheus!

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.490
We don’t need to lose
any more people over this!

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:10.000
The Two of Us!

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.300
Auxiliary battery: Connected.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.100
Energy status: Fully charged.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.560
We’re all set now!

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.630
Let’s hurry and meet up with Kaito!

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.690
Now we have to figure out how to
get inside Amgine, don’t we?

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:23.760
That won’t be a problem.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.530
I’ll disable Amgine’s
air defenses, during which

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.770
time we’ll bulldoze our way in and land.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.280
Now to start hacking their system!

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.450
Midflight POG jet! Midflight POG jet!

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.460
This is the Amgine International
Airport Control Room.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.880
I would like to deliver a
message from the President.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.260
“Welcome to the Republic of Amgine.”

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:49.910
“You are welcome here.”

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:54.180
“Follow our instructions and swiftly
proceed through immigrations.”

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.420
I repeat...

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.310
Kaito, what the heck happened?!

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:00.940
Tell me, Kaito!

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.180
Hey, where are Gammon and Freecell?

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:05.180
Sorry...

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.180
Please leave me alone.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:09.320
Kaito!

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.250
Ah, there they are!

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:13.310
Cube! Guys!

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.310
Nonoha, where is Kaito?

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:21.120
Kaito! It’s me, Kaito!

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.660
I did it! I made an
anti-Orpheus secret weapon!

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:29.170
The moment Orpheus tries to
transfer his mind into yours,

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:31.510
we can block him with a special radio pulse!

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:34.330
If all goes well, we might be
able to save everyone!

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.140
Kaito...?

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.840
It looks like something must have happened.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:45.840
Gammon and Freecell never came
back from their last puzzle.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:48.950
The ship was on fire...

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.950
I hope Gammon isn’t...

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.870
Not to worry. Both of them are fine.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.370
Mr. Principal! When did you come to Amgine?

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.230
Before you.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:03.430
I received word
that Kaito and the others

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.740
had been invited aboard
the President’s yacht.

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:09.990
To play it safe,
I placed a rescue team on standby.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:12.840
I never expected him to
blow up the entire ship.

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:15.240
When we rescued Mr. Gammon and

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:17.750
Mr. Freecell, they had
sustained minor injuries.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.060
As such, the POG is looking after them.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:23.980
They are currently receiving
treatment overseas,

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.810
but both of them are okay!

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.400
Really?!

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:31.000
That’s a relief! That’s a relief!

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.450
He got hurt?

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.840
I was wondering why he
suddenly stopped texting me.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.400
So that’s the deal!

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.900
Melancholy, you’re here too?

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.150
I swear, he is always giving
me cause for concern!

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:48.180
But it sounds like I
didn’t need to rush over

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.780
on my Pretty Melancholy Submarine after all!

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:53.130
You and Freecell have
been texting each other?

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.040
Since when?

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:57.540
Goodness! You don’t know
EVERYTHING about him after all.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.890
I’m glad that he made
a friend aside from me,

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.890
but it wasn’t very nice of Freecell
to keep me in the dark!

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:06.320
I’ll have to give him a piece of my mind.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:12.300
Mr. Principal, have you heard
word from Director Rook?

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.180
I haven’t been able to
get in touch with him.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:19.280
Really? You didn’t receive the message?

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.630
He’ll be acting independently
since he’d like

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:23.210
to investigate something on his own,

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:25.080
but he doesn’t want
anyone to worry about him.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.570
That’s what the Director’s message said.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.960
Really? You don’t say!

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.300
I’m glad he’s okay!

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.800
How wonderful! How wonderful!

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.670
How wonderful! How wonderful!

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:40.250
“Gammon and Freecell are
both all right,” huh?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:44.930
Could you please tell me
the truth, Mr. Principal?

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:48.260
As I feared, I couldn’t
hide the truth from you.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:52.060
I am doing everything within my
power to search for them,

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.610
but no one has claimed to find them yet.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:56.020
And Director Rook?

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:01.240
Several days ago,
he asked to see Kaito in Amgine.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.110
After that, he went missing.

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:07.870
Upon looking into it, we found a large,
underground battle puzzle.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:13.780
The two faced off with this puzzle and
Director Rook lost. He is most likely...

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.040
Why did you lie to everyone?

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:20.390
If they knew the truth,

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:23.280
they would probably try to stop Kaito so he

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:26.050
wouldn’t work with puzzles anymore.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.520
But it is imperative that Kaito challenge

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:32.150
the Puzzle of God if we hope to stop Orpheus.

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:37.060
The less noise there is to disturb
his heart... the better.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:42.060
Are you trying to dump all of the
responsibility onto Kaito?!

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:45.840
As it is, all of our problems
revolving around the Puzzle of God

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.320
go back to you and Jin!

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:50.720
I am well aware that what I am doing makes

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.390
me a horrible adult--no, a horrible person.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:56.130
But do you know of any other way?

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:59.950
You and I aren’t even capable
of becoming Phi-Brains!

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:06.460
Mr. Principle, I am going to help
search for Gammon and the others.

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:12.220
Even if I can’t become a Phi-Brain,
I want to help in every way I possibly can!

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.970
Nonoha, they’re done!

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:21.160
These are stamina cookies for Kaito...

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:24.230
These are energy macarons for the injured.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.490
Why must I do this?!

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:29.290
Stop talking and keep those hands moving!

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:31.820
Those are important sweets
for when we visit Freecell!

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:34.500
They will start the Puzzle of God soon.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:38.500
As the girls’ team, let’s
do what we can to help!

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.090
Yeah!

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:45.330
But not only is the Puzzle of God
insanely difficult,

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:48.460
we don’t know what will happen
to the winner or the loser.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:50.390
Will Kaito be all right?

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.330
That’s a given!

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:55.190
Gammon and Freecell
both survived that last one.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:57.470
I’m sure this next one
will work out okay, too!

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.350
I certainly hope so.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:00.350
Huh?

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:03.600
I mean, hasn’t he been locked up
in his room since he got back?

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.530
Kaito Daimon, that is.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:06.850
Y-yeah...

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:11.660
Gammon...

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.500
Freecell...

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:15.240
Rook...

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:24.200
This feels like a walk down memory lane...

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:27.560
I used to come here a lot when
I was traveling with Jin.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.330
Wait for me, Jin!

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.330
This all comes to an end tomorrow!

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:35.350
I swear that I will save you.

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:39.390
I’ll solve the Puzzle of God by myself.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.890
Raetsel, don’t show up!

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:43.990
Kaito...

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:45.490
Aw, damn it!

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:47.910
I’m going for it again!

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.580
Big Brother!

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:51.190
I’ve gotta get them!

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:53.690
They’re going to be my
birthday present to Dad!

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:54.870
All right!

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:57.040
You won’t get them like that, Big Brother!

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:59.340
You need to aim higher...

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:01.130
Shut up! Keep your opinion to yourself!

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:03.340
Stop that! You shouldn’t
fight with each other!

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:06.120
What are you doing?! Give that back!

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:08.460
Hmm. So that’s what you’re after.

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:12.480
In that case, you should
take your sister’s advice.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.390
Um, uh...

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:17.970
Let’s get them together, Big Brother!

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:22.470
Yeah, you’re right.
That’d make Dad happier too, wouldn’t it?

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:25.650
Uh, I’m supposed to aim for
the top of the pole, right?

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:26.480
Uh-huh!

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:28.480
Like this?

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:30.200
Hold it a bit higher.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.230
All right!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:34.870
I got them!

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:36.290
We did it! We did it!

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:36.830
“Together,” huh?

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.030
We got them!
“Together,” huh?

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:40.750
Congratulations.
Here are the sunglasses you won.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.670
Yay! Hurray! Hurray!

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:51.770
Raetsel?

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.550
Kaito will like them, won’t he?

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:57.550
If he utters a word of complaint,
I will throttle him for you!

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:04.900
Kaito, I’m coming in.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:07.680
Three, two, one! Yay!

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:12.650
Tada! Everyone worked together to
bake some pick-me-up--Huh?

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.290
He isn’t here?

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:18.740
What’s the deal?!
And here we baked him some sweets.

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:30.250
I can’t decide!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.330
All of the stalls have
such good-looking food.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:34.520
Ah, this might be nice!

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:35.840
Mister, I’d like two.

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:37.350
Sure thing!

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:38.810
Come back again!

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:43.430
What are you up to, Raetsel?

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:46.180
I can’t stand to see you looking like this.

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:50.240
As you are now, you wouldn’t
stand a chance against me.

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:52.320
I’m not going to face you.

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:55.110
I already told you to back out
of the Puzzle of God!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:58.120
I’m the one who awoke Orpheus.

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:00.610
So I’ll take Orpheus down on my own!

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:02.860
His challenge to the gods...

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:07.720
I’ve lost so much over his stupid goal!

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.310
I don’t want to lose anyone--

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:14.010
You’re making a scene, sheesh!

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:17.310
And he thinks you transcended
beyond human emotions?

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.380
Orpheus just doesn’t get it!

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:24.690
Kaito Daimon, there is no way I could
lose to you as you are now!

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:28.070
No, the current you couldn’t
even solve a puzzle.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:31.700
I mean, your eyes are dead right now.

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:35.200
You weren’t ready to lose any of the

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.750
people you care about, were you?

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:41.530
But... there’s nothing wrong with that.

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:44.780
After all, you’re human.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:48.170
I could never imagine the pain
you’re going through.

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:51.540
You’ve had to endure abandoning
your beloved friends.

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.150
Tell me, Kaito...

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:58.960
Why are you willing to go to such lengths
to challenge the Puzzle of God?

00:13:02.390 --> 00:13:04.400
I’m doing it to save Jin.

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.180
Are you doing it to defeat Orpheus?

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.490
Or are you doing it to protect
those you hold dear?

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:13.950
I...

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:16.150
Leeks?

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:17.990
Doesn’t this have leeks?

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.000
That’s okay.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.650
Amgine’s leeks are so soft,
sweet and delicious

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.650
that even I can eat them.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:29.160
You’re right!

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:31.920
I’m glad to hear you agree!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:32.660
Huh?

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:34.920
Remember what Nonoha said?

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.420
“Most problems can be resolved
once you’ve eaten a good meal.”

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:43.420
Yeah, and these leeks are definitely good.

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:44.780
Aren’t they?

00:13:45.730 --> 00:13:47.400
Why am I doing this, huh?

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:49.800
Thank you, Raetsel.

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.680
I had lost sight
of somethin’ important!

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.590
If Gammon and Freecell were here to see me,

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:57.560
I woulda gotten whacked again!

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:03.410
Puzzles are chains. Puzzles are mirrors.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:07.290
You and I are opposite sides
of the mirror held together

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.990
by the chain called Jin.

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:11.140
We aren’t buddies,

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:14.660
but there are some things that can only
be accomplished if we work together.

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:17.300
Let’s face it together, Kaito!

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:20.630
In order to protect those we care about,
let’s challenge it together!

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:21.990
Yeah!

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:29.390
Cube, any luck?

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:32.140
None at all! I couldn’t find him anywhere.

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:32.140
He’s gone! He’s gone!

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:36.490
Why won’t he tell us anything?
Kaito’s such a moron!

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:37.320
My bad!

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:39.770
Kaito!

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:42.040
Thank you, Nonoha!

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:47.030
Sure enough, your Nonoha Sweets are great!

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.520
Cubik, I heard you made a secret weapon.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:53.280
Thank you!

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:56.040
You’re welcome. You’re welcome.

00:14:56.510 --> 00:15:00.420
Principal, Upperclassman, guys...
I’m sorry for everything.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:01.920
Kaito...

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:06.300
Tomorrow we’re going to
challenge the Puzzle of God!

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:10.800
I promise that I will protect your futures.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:14.280
And I’ll be sure to come back!

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:17.810
Jin, Raetsel and I will come back together!

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:19.310
Kaito!

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:24.320
Then that settles it! Now let’s eat these.

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:25.290
What are “these”?

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:27.500
The sweets that we baked.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.070
You guys cooked?

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.170
Bite your tongue!

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:34.330
Rae-Rae, you made him feel better,
didn’t you? Kaito, that is.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:35.480
Ana!

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:38.580
I, Ana, think we should thank you!

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:40.550
Let’s go, Rae-Rae!

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:42.210
Wait!

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.210
Guys!

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:44.710
Raetsel!

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:47.770
I-I was just leaving.

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:49.810
Don’t! Spend the night.

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:52.820
Aren’t you facing the
Puzzle of God together?

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:54.970
But...

00:15:55.400 --> 00:16:00.070
Miss Raetsel, I’ve been wanting
a chance to talk to you.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:02.230
It looks like we share similar interests!

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:06.900
With Raetsel here, doesn’t this remind
you of our girls’ day out?

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.460
Huh? You had one?

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:11.400
Doesn’t it?

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.790
Uh, yeah...

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:17.200
No fair! I wanna girls’ day out or a party!

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:18.990
My, that sounds like fun.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.500
Please show her a super good time!

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:24.100
It’ll be my pleasure!

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:27.310
Ladies, we’re moving to the girls’ room!

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:28.270
Yeah!

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:30.760
H-hey! What gives?!

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:36.010
I would hereby like to begin the
Second Girls’ Party... in Amgine!

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:37.760
Yay!

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:41.520
Wow! It’s a girls’ party! A girls’ party!
Clap, clap, clap, clap!

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.870
Um, I...

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:46.700
Stop worrying and drink up.
It’s strawberry juice!

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:49.790
It’s important to have a gap!

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:52.500
For example, you look cool,
but you’re actually pure in heart.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:53.960
Like Rae-Rae?

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:55.630
Ah, I totally get what you mean!

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:59.510
Or so she says. What are
your thoughts, Raetsel?

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:02.680
I-I don’t think that’s the case...

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:05.510
You look great! Really great!

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:07.920
Too cute!

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:10.550
Rae-Rae!

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:14.630
Now you’re asking for it!

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:20.150
No! You’re supposed to pull that.

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:23.490
No! Why are you pushing that?

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:25.920
No, no! What are you doing?

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:28.610
Looking there won’t help you any.

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:31.030
I can’t!

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:35.000
What have you done?!

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.860
You’re unbelievable!

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.450
Honestly, why are you
all thumbs with puzzles?

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:40.710
Am not! This one started out--

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:43.950
You’re hilarious!
You guys really are fun to watch.

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:48.270
It must be nice... You’re
such good friends.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.810
Rae-Rae, you’re included
in our circle of friends.

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:51.990
Huh?

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:54.470
Everyone is also friends with Rae-Rae!

00:17:56.900 --> 00:18:02.470
Not just anyone could don that
Armlet for the person they love.

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:06.530
I’d like to hold many,
many more conversations with you.

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:09.730
Same here! So please be sure
to come back to us!

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.980
Let’s keep these girls’ parties going!

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:15.770
Guys...

00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:24.260
Gammon...

00:18:25.090 --> 00:18:27.640
Freecell, you dummy!

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:31.100
You’ve shown yourself at last, scoundrel!

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:39.060
“All I have is Jin.”

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:41.210
“All I need is Jin.”

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:43.060
That’s what I used to think.

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:47.810
Everyone is also friends with Rae-Rae!

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:50.370
That made me happy.

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:55.950
It was delightful, delicious and fun.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.840
It was as wonderful as my memories of Jin...

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:09.970
Thank you, everyone.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.370
Raetsel...

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:28.230
I, Ana, think we’ll see her again!

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.700
We made a promise!

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.990
All systems: All green.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:36.530
Standby: Complete.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.580
Okay! Let’s go, Kaito.

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:40.030
That’s the robot, isn’t it?

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:44.910
Isn’t it the one standing between me
and my reunion with Lovushka?

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:47.300
Zagadka!

00:19:47.590 --> 00:19:48.430
Carry it away.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:49.660
Huh? Wait!

00:19:52.510 --> 00:19:54.040
Wh-what are you doing?!

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:54.040
D-Doctor!

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.170
Doctor!

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:56.920
Iwashimizu!

00:19:57.810 --> 00:19:59.050
I’ll be back!

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:04.320
Now shall we go, Kaito Daimon,
to the Puzzle of God?

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:07.060
I’m off, guys!

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:10.180
Make sure you come back, Kaito!

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:12.690
Yeah!

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:25.700
This is... the Puzzle of God...

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:30.120
Phi-Brain children, are you ready?

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:30.950
Yeah!

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:31.960
Yes!

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:02.820
What on earth... is this?

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:12.890
What type of puzzle is this?! Orpheus!

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:17.000
You must discover the rules for yourselves.

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:18.250
Damn it!

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:22.310
It is just like how you must find
your own purpose in life.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:26.760
Let’s commence... Puzzle of God time!

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:33.200
I’m the color red. I should go there next!

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:37.490
You increase your territory as you move...

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.000
It’s a puzzle where we steal
each other’s territory.

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:48.370
So that’s the past they chose.

00:21:57.970 --> 00:22:01.850
This is... the house I
lived in a long time ago.

00:22:11.150 --> 00:22:14.200
What is this about, Orpheus?!

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:19.390
This puzzle has transcended time and space.

00:22:19.790 --> 00:22:21.230
It is the Time Maze!

00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:25.680
Change your past and seize...

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:28.760
the future where you become a Phi-Brain!

00:24:01.930 --> 00:24:03.540
I can see it!

00:24:04.100 --> 00:24:06.480
I can see who will awaken as a Phi-Brain

00:24:06.890 --> 00:24:10.690
and who will spend all eternity
wandering the Time Maze.

00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:14.720
It is up to you who I choose.

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:19.380
Change your past and seize your futures!

00:24:20.030 --> 00:24:22.300
Next time, “Even If
Something’s Missing.”

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:27.980
Even If Something’s Missing

00:24:22.780 --> 00:24:26.320
Now, let’s commence... Puzzle of God time!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin
Art: Akeru Otsuki
